<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ekkathat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1767">1767</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ekkathat was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a>, reigning from 1758 to 1767 after his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uthumphon">Uthumphon</a> gave up the throne. Weak and faction-ridden, his court could not resist the Konbaung armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, which besieged the capital from 1766 and sacked it in April 1767; Ekkathat died during or shortly after its fall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ekkathat.jpg" alt="Ekkathat" width="320" height="588" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FrameHotep · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KingEkkathat_Wat_Lamud_Ayutthaya_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
